### Corrections and deliberate changes

These are not attributed to Sher as if they were in the original implementation.

| Source detail                                                          | Treatment here                                                                                                   |
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Neuron termination is spelled `termiante` twice on p. 177              | Use supervisor-owned shutdown rather than copy the misspelled message                                            |
| Cortex sends another sensor sync before decrementing to zero on p. 177 | Complete each requested cycle before returning; never start an unrequested final cycle                           |
| `random` and timestamp-derived floating-point IDs                      | Explicit `:rand` state and deterministic local IDs                                                               |
| Registered names `neuron` and `cortex` in the early examples           | Pass PIDs explicitly so independent networks can coexist                                                         |
| Broad pipeline possibility on pp. 163-164                              | Keep one cycle in flight; pipelining is not implemented                                                          |
| Record list, ETS ID/PID lookup, textual file storage                   | Maps retain record fields; immutable maps provide lookup; versioned binary stores the genotype                   |
| `rng` inside each sensor process                                       | Generate once, then replay the same observations for controlled comparison                                       |
| Actuator prints every result                                           | Collect results for tests and timing; demonstrate `pts/1` explicitly                                             |
| Backup anticipates learning                                            | Retain the path, but do not claim weights were learned in this static chapter                                    |
| Source constructor supports only `rng` width 2 and `pts` width 1       | Keep that compatibility entry point; add explicit dimensions for comparison tests                                |
| Cortex described as potentially supervisory                            | Separate synchronization from OTP ownership; fail-stop and rebuild rather than claim automatic in-place recovery |

The source explicitly converts `{:bias, value}` into a standalone runtime bias
on p. 183. That is a representation conversion, **not** a defect being corrected.
The two concrete control-flow issues above are visible in the printed listing;
this notebook does not claim to have audited a different repository version.

